  * Natural Earth 1:50m Admin-0 country boundaries
    (https://www.naturalearthdata.com, version 5.1.2) — bundled as
    app/data/country_borders.geojson for the OSM geographic-scope feature
    and the country of a stop in the station module's stop extract: the
    European countries and Turkey, and the countries beyond their land
    borders (Armenia, Azerbaijan, Brazil, China, Georgia, Iran, Iraq, Japan,
    Kazakhstan, Mongolia, North Korea, Suriname, Syria), with their
    coordinates as published (the 1:50m scale is coarse: borders up to some
    3 km off). Gibraltar is Natural Earth's 1:10m polygon (absent at 1:50m).
    Changes made: ISO codes normalised where Natural Earth gives -99 (France
    FR, Norway NO, Kosovo XK; XK is a user-assigned code, not ISO 3166-1);
    Crimea is Ukraine's, the EU position (Natural Earth's points of view
    for Ukraine and the EU members it covers; its breakaway/disputed area
    "Crimea", whose 1:50m polygon is the one moved from Russia to Ukraine).
    Public domain; no attribution required, credited here as a courtesy.

  * app/data/country_borders_v1_patch.geojson (issue #404), the finer
    borders between the countries offered for the OSM crop, within 10 km
    of their land borders with each other, used for the country of a stop
    in the station module's stop extract. Built by
    scripts/build_v1_border_patch.py, which records each source's URL,
    version and sha256, from:
    - geoBoundaries CGAZ ADM0 (www.geoboundaries.org; GitHub
      wmgeolab/geoBoundaries, commit
      5c25134028196d43ce97b5071934fd0cfc92f09f). Runfola, D. et al. (2020)
      geoBoundaries: A global database of political administrative
      boundaries. PLoS ONE 15(4): e0231866.
      https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0231866
      Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
      License (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
      Its international boundaries are those of the U.S. Department of
      State's Large Scale International Boundaries (LSIB), a work of the
      U.S. Government in the public domain.
    - Natural Earth 1:10m land (https://www.naturalearthdata.com, version
      5.1.2), public domain: the land and the coast.
    Changes made: only the land within 10 km of those borders (and Borkum
    and a shore of the Flensburg Fjord, which the 1:50m file gives to the
    neighbour) is kept, with 2 km of sea along Natural Earth's coast,
    divided between the countries by CGAZ's boundaries (land CGAZ leaves
    out going to the nearest country); CGAZ's own coasts are not kept;
    Gibraltar and the Sovereign Base Areas on Cyprus are not counted as
    the United Kingdom; simplified at 200 m (mapshaper, topology kept) and
    rounded to 5 decimals.

  * MapLibre GL JS (when wired in step 14 of the implementation order)
    Licensed under the BSD-3-Clause License.

